<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Default language: Persian.

  Two number rules, and they are not the same rule. A figure a reader compares against a server, a
  broker or another log stays Latin — a status code, a duration in milliseconds, a version, a byte
  count, a base URL. A count in a sentence is prose and takes Persian digits, which is why the
  counters below are formatted with %1$s rather than %1$d: the digits are converted before they
  arrive, and a `%d` would print Latin ones straight into a Persian phrase.
-->
<resources>

